# Dates in Russian history: в 1703 году, в XVIII веке
subtitle: "Say when things happened in Russian history: два́дцать седьмо́го ма́я ты́сяча семьсо́т тре́тьего го́да, в восемна́дцатом ве́ке, в нача́ле ве́ка, с … по …"
tags: ["russian","russian dates","years in russian","russian history","petersburg"]
teaches: ["grammar/number-cases","phrases/dates","vocabulary/history"]
thumb: "band \"Say 1703 like a Russian\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would","b":"gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated"}
next: {"title":"A Russian radio interview: have you ever cooked borscht?","href":"https://www.drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/drawcast-library/russian-from-zero/156-russian-radio-interview.cast"}

